# broiler-js-conformance retained suite pin 1
#
# A pin this repository holds for a suite it does not hold. `revision` is the immutable upstream
# commit roadmap section 14 asks for - "never a branch name" - and `content-sha256` is the digest
# the harness computes over every path and content the checkout of that revision produces, its own
# pin file excepted.
#
# WHY THE AUTHORITY IS HERE AND NOT IN THE CHECKOUT. `--pin` writes a digest into the directory it
# just read, which is right for a suite this repository holds and worth nothing for one it does
# not: a `suite.pin` generated inside a third-party checkout says the directory has not changed
# since the harness last looked at it, and says nothing about which upstream revision it is.
# Whoever can edit the suite can edit that pin in the same gesture. This file cannot be reached
# from the suite, so a run given `--expect` has to match something decided here.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. Retrieved twice on 2026-09-03, from the codeload archive of the named commit,
# into two directories; the two downloads were byte-identical and the second was extracted into a
# fresh directory and hashed independently of the first, which is what makes `content-sha256` a
# reading rather than a copy of an earlier reading.
#
# WHAT IS HERE, SINCE 2026-09-03. The suite, as the archive it was retrieved as: one file of
# 9,487,173 bytes hashing to `archive-sha256` below, which extracts to the 56,560 files
# `content-sha256` is over. The extracted form is 232 megabytes and was not chosen: this repository
# packs to a few megabytes and one file at four per cent of the size carries the same evidence,
# which is that a reader can check the digest without asking a network. It is separately licensed
# under the BSD 3-Clause terms retained beside this file.

suite test262
upstream tc39/test262
revision ccaac100ff49d81e9ff47a75ff4c60e0bd3f262e
